00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Slow JOIN or GROUP BY?
Check the shuffle.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Shuffle = regroup data across partitions
Usually copied across executors and machines

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,500
9 orders, 3 partitions
GROUP BY customer_id

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,000
All A rows must meet

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Map side: route rows by key
target = hash(key) mod N

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Illustrative: A→R0, B→R1, C→R2

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Reduce side: fetch your blocks
Each task pulls its blocks from the map outputs

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Often over the network

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Now each key is in one place
A = 21 · B = 32 · C = 23

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Why it's expensive:
disk I/O + serialization + network I/O

11
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,000
Spills add more disk and GC

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,500
Small side? Broadcast it (auto ≤ 10 MB by default)
AQE merges small shuffle partitions

13
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:39,000
AQE splits skewed join partitions

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,500
Shuffle = rows regrouped across partitions
usually across machines

